<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia allocates 3.6 million barrels Nov LSWR.</title>
<headline>Indonesia allocates 3.6 million barrels Nov LSWR.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company, Pertamina has allocated a total of 3.6 million barrels of low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) for loading in November, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>Pertamina has yet to give full details of the loading schedule, a Japanese trader told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Pertamina has also rolled over 400,000 barrels of LSWR from October,&quot; another Japanese trader said.</p>
<p>The volumes rolled over from last month will bring Pertamina total allocation in November to 4 million barrels, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082).</p>
